WEBVTT

00:15.300 --> 00:17.665
So code is no longer the bottleneck.

00:18.415 --> 00:22.816
Anthropic's playbook for delivering
software with agents has six stages.

00:22.916 --> 00:27.580
Plan, design, build, test, deploy,
maintain.

00:27.680 --> 00:29.566
Agents now run all six.

00:29.916 --> 00:31.197
Look at stage four.

00:31.297 --> 00:34.091
The agent checks itself, with a test it
wrote.

00:34.191 --> 00:35.261
Hold that thought.

00:36.011 --> 00:37.144
Here's the catch.

00:37.244 --> 00:39.388
This test was written by an agent.

00:39.488 --> 00:41.853
It ran, and it's green.

00:41.953 --> 00:43.082
And it's wrong.

00:43.182 --> 00:45.277
It checks the app against the app.

00:45.377 --> 00:47.036
Green is not correct.

00:47.986 --> 00:49.510
So what's our new goal?

00:49.610 --> 00:51.952
If you build, you shape the work.

00:52.052 --> 00:54.391
If you automate, you maintain it.

00:54.491 --> 00:56.962
If you test, you define the rules.

00:57.062 --> 01:00.121
If you lead, you manage the whole process.

01:00.221 --> 01:03.150
A role or a skill? Nobody knows yet.

01:03.800 --> 01:05.772
Will AI replace testers?

01:05.872 --> 01:07.305
Not the ones who are ready.

01:07.405 --> 01:10.048
Agents will do more and more of the
testing.

01:10.148 --> 01:15.324
This series gets you ready, with free,
hands-on labs and the tools teams use now.

01:15.974 --> 01:19.488
Every tutorial on this page gives you the
same four things.

01:19.588 --> 01:21.642
A short video with one idea.

01:21.742 --> 01:24.642
A lab in your browser, with nothing to
install.

01:24.742 --> 01:27.493
An automatic check that grades what you
built.

01:27.593 --> 01:31.074
And a certificate when you pass, free like
everything else.

01:31.624 --> 01:33.328
Here's roughly what we're building.

01:33.428 --> 01:37.612
We start with agentic testing, MCP and
skills.

01:37.712 --> 01:43.038
Then Playwright, API testing, test data,
and how far you can trust an agent's

01:43.078 --> 01:43.952
verdict.

01:43.992 --> 01:46.265
All the way to rolling it out in your
team.

01:46.365 --> 01:50.880
We'll shape and improve it as we learn, so
the final list may look a bit different.

01:50.980 --> 01:54.611
The goal stays the same: get you ready to
lead the agents.

01:55.361 --> 01:57.434
Get ready to lead the agents.

01:57.534 --> 01:59.921
Pick a tutorial below and open the lab.
